module gunbc.rung_drop.spark_serving_local_artifact_not_reproducible

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, AuthoredProse, SparkServingLocalArtifactNotReproducible }

data spark_serving_local_artifact_not_reproducible: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "spark_serving_local_artifact_not_reproducible" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "Reproduction of a Spark serving group's model artifact from desired state",

  declared: "2026-09-02",

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: AuthoredProse { legacy: SparkServingLocalArtifactNotReproducible, authored: "Spark serving model materialization — **RUNG DROP, DECLARED (2026-09-02).** SUBJECT: the ability to reconstruct a serving cell's model artifact from desired state alone. WHAT WAS HELD: while `gunbc.spark.serving_desired` `spark_serving_desired_manifest` selected an upstream library tag, `gunbc.spark.serving_converge_realize` `spark_serving_materialize_model_artifact_steps` emitted a complete fetch-and-verify install plan — manifest fetched by reference, checked against the frozen resolved digest, every blob in the closure fetched by digest, staged, verified and only then published. A cell with an empty model store could be converged into a serving one. WHAT IS LOST: desired state now selects `deepseek-v4-gguf:no-h3-stop`, which was produced by `POST /api/create` ON THE CELLS THEMSELVES and has no registry anywhere. The materializer REFUSES for it, so convergence can verify and serve the artifact but cannot rebuild it: a cell that lost its model store cannot be restored by this plan. WHY THE REFUSAL IS NOT ITSELF THE DEFECT: the alternative was emitting `curl` against a registry path that never existed, which fails at apply time on a real host with a transport error that reads as a network fault rather than as the category error it is; and the OTHER alternative — silently degrading to a verify-only plan — is the absorbing fallback, actuating as 'nothing to do' against a host with nothing installed. The line stops, typed and located, naming the producer. WHAT REMAINS: the upstream arm is untouched and still executes its full sequence, and stays enrolled as executing evidence via `test.claim.spark_serving_model_materialization_witness`, which now names `gpt_oss_120b_manifest` explicitly rather than reading desired state — precisely so this arm does not become green-by-vacuity while unselected. PREVIOUS RUNG: mechanically preventable. TEMPORARY RUNG: mitigatable — the gap is refused rather than silent, but the artifact's existence on the cells is an external fact this repository observes and cannot reproduce. RESTORATION TRIGGER — THE CAPABILITY, NOT AN ARTIFACT: a locally materialized manifest can be CONSTRUCTED by the convergence plan from facts this repository owns — the parent artifact's identity and blob closure, and the transformation applied to it — such that a cell with an empty model store converges to the byte-identical resolved identity without a human running `ollama create`. Modeling the Modelfile alone does NOT discharge this row: the plan must construct the artifact and the resulting identity must be checkable against the frozen resolution, or the same unreproducible state persists behind a row that reads as covered. RE-ANCHORED 2026-09-06: the Ollama-era tree this was declared over was deleted; the population is now the vLLM group model's weight snapshot (gunbc.spark.pair_serving_realization binds the HF hub cache read-only at /weights), which group B received by a hand-run copy over the fabric rail on 2026-09-05 and no desired row materializes. The restoration trigger is unchanged: a desired row that materializes the artifact by digest on a host that lacks it. PARTIALLY ADVANCED 2026-09-07, AND THE TRIGGER IS STILL NOT DISCHARGED -- which is the point of recording it here rather than closing the row. `gunbc.spark.model_snapshot_acquisition` now carries a desired row per model, pinned to a resolved upstream commit (DeepSeek at 60d8d707..., GLM-5.3-Flash at eb9eb208..., the latter resolved from the Hub model API on 2026-09-07), and `gunbc.artifact_acquisition` is the subject-agnostic upsert that brings one to a host it is missing from. So a host with an empty model store is no longer unreachable from desired state, and the hand-run rail copy of 2026-09-05 has a modelled replacement. WHAT IS STILL MISSING IS EXACTLY THE WORD `by digest`: the acquisition is keyed on `UpstreamRevision`, not on a content digest this repository holds, so integrity is DELEGATED to the transport (`hf cache verify` checks the cached files against the Hub own checksums, which is a real per-file check but is upstream answering at verification time rather than an oracle frozen here). `gunbc.artifact_acquisition acquisition_key_is_locally_verifiable` answers false for that key, so the weakening is a declared property a consumer can branch on rather than an implication. The remaining step is named and reachable: `extdeps.huggingface.hub hub_repo_tree_api_url` is the observation that yields a per-file sha256 manifest, at which point every shard becomes its own ContentDigestSha256 subject over the same combinator and nothing changes shape. It is not built because a manifest of that size is an observation and hand-authoring one is the fabrication this repository refuses. SEPARATELY UNRESOLVED, and not a modeling gap: which transport moves the bytes. The 2026-09-05 copy went over the fabric rail rather than the management LAN, and nothing has decided which the modelled acquisition should use." }
}
